A turn's virtual time moves on a count for each count it ran, whatever its payer's units, rather than TIME_UNITS / units.
A thread with few units would run as long a request as one with the whole core;
a turn costs its payer TIME_UNITS / units counts for each count, rounded up.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: a step of the clock did not charge the thread whose turn it was its units' part
Report: a traced call that moved no time charged the thread whose turn it was
Witness: fuzz bind-turn-later

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -378,7 +378,7 @@ static uint64_t turn_vtime(const struct core *core, const struct place *p, uint6
     if (p->vt >= bound) {
         return p->vt;
     }
-    uint64_t cost = units_divide((now - core->turn_from) * TIME_UNITS + units - 1, units);
+    uint64_t cost = units_divide((now - core->turn_from) * TIME_UNITS + units - 1, TIME_UNITS);
     return cost < bound - p->vt ? p->vt + cost : bound;
 }
 
